  "series": "TERRAFORM STATE: FIELD NOTES",
  "date": "07/09/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What State Is and Why It Exists",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "State is a JSON map from config addresses (`aws_instance.web`) to real object IDs (`i-0abc123`). It also caches that object's attributes."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "config",
              "state map",
              "provider",
              "real infra"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cloud APIs can't say which of 400 instances is yours",
            "No cross-provider ownership tag standard exists",
            "So Terraform records the binding itself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Jobs of State"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Job",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "identity map",
              "config ↔ real ID"
            ],
            [
              "attribute cache",
              "no N API reads"
            ],
            [
              "dependency order",
              "correct destroy"
            ],
            [
              "outputs",
              "other configs read"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Declarative but not stateless",
            "No state = apply recreates everything",
            "Nothing else links config to reality"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why Store the Graph"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "On destroy, resources are gone from config",
            "Old graph knows subnet dies after its instance",
            "Recomputing from a deleted config is impossible"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Files on Disk"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform.tfstate         # working dir",
            "terraform.tfstate.backup  # prior write",
            "terraform.tfstate.d/staging/  # workspace",
            "terraform plan -refresh=false # cache only"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`terraform workspace new staging` = separate state",
            "Remote backends key the workspace into the path",
            "Same config, isolated state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Hard Rules",
          "items": [
            "Never hand-edit `terraform.tfstate`",
            "`serial` + `lineage` + schemas must stay consistent",
            "One root module = one state = one lock",
            "One state = one blast radius"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "What State Is and Why It Exists (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Belief vs Reality",
          "text": "State is what Terraform believes exists. Reality is what does exist. The gap is drift."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Lost the state file — is my infra gone?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "No. State is not a backup of infrastructure",
            "You lost the mapping, not the resources",
            "They keep running, orphaned and unmanaged",
            "Re-import by ID to rebuild the map"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Address Is the Key"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "# rename web -> api, no state move",
            "resource \"aws_instance\" \"api\" {}",
            "# plan: -/+ destroy and create",
            "# 5000 resources = plans in minutes"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Top-Level Fields",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{ \"version\": 4,",
            "  \"terraform_version\": \"1.9.5\",",
            "  \"serial\": 87, \"lineage\": \"3f2a-...\",",
            "  \"outputs\": {}, \"resources\": [],",
            "  \"check_results\": null }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`serial`",
              "bumped every write"
            ],
            [
              "`lineage`",
              "UUID at creation"
            ],
            [
              "`version`",
              "on-disk format, 4"
            ],
            [
              "`terraform_version`",
              "last writer binary"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Remote backends reject writes with a stale `serial`",
            "Different lineage = unrelated state, refused without `-force`",
            "Older binaries refuse newer state; upgrades are one-way"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "resources[] Entries"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`mode`: \"managed\" or \"data\"",
            "`type`, `name`, and full `provider` address",
            "`instances[]` holds the actual objects"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "matrix",
          "spec": {
            "rows": [
              [
                "schema_version",
                "attributes"
              ],
              [
                "dependencies",
                "private"
              ],
              [
                "index_key"
              ]
            ],
            "caption": "one instance"
          }
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anatomy of the State File",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`index_key`: int for `count`, string for `for_each`",
            "That is why count→for_each forces address changes",
            "`attributes` holds computed ARNs, IDs, DNS names",
            "Interpolation reads them with zero API calls"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`private`: opaque base64 provider blob",
            "Holds timeouts and create-before-destroy bookkeeping",
            "`dependencies`: addresses resolved at apply time",
            "Destroy order survives deleting the config"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Outputs and Deposed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`outputs` stores `value` plus a `sensitive` flag",
            "`terraform_remote_state` reads exactly this section",
            "Failed create_before_destroy parks the old object",
            "It lands under a `deposed` key with a random ID"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Inspect, Never Edit"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform state list        # addresses",
            "terraform state show aws_instance.web",
            "terraform show -json | jq \\",
            "  '.values.root_module.resources[].address'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Not a Public API",
          "text": "Raw state JSON is internal. The documented, versioned interface is `terraform show -json`."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Plaintext Secrets",
          "items": [
            "`sensitive = true` does not encrypt anything",
            "It only masks CLI output",
            "Passwords and keys sit in state as plain JSON",
            "Clearing a deposed object needs `-force`"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Inputs to a Plan",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "config (desired)",
              "state (last known)",
              "refresh (actual)",
              "diff"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Refresh, Plan, Apply",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Refresh calls the provider's ReadResource per managed resource",
            "It passes the stored ID, gets live attributes back",
            "Cached attributes are replaced with the answer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Refresh Flags"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "default",
              "in-memory since 0.15.4"
            ],
            [
              "`-refresh-only`",
              "state moves, infra doesn't"
            ],
            [
              "`-refresh=false`",
              "no reads, stale attrs"
            ],
            [
              "`terraform refresh`",
              "deprecated command"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefer `terraform apply -refresh-only` over `refresh`",
            "`-refresh=false` saves huge states from rate limits",
            "Cost: the plan is built on stale values"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Diff Outcomes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Four per resource: no-op, update, replace, destroy",
            "Replacement is forced by `ForceNew` schema attributes",
            "Refresh returning null drops it from state",
            "It then reappears in the plan as a create"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symbol",
            "Action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`+`",
              "create"
            ],
            [
              "`-`",
              "destroy"
            ],
            [
              "`~`",
              "update in place"
            ],
            [
              "`-/+`",
              "replace"
            ],
            [
              "`<=`",
              "read data source"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Escape Hatches"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -target=aws_instance.web",
            "terraform apply -replace=aws_instance.web",
            "# -replace superseded `terraform taint`",
            "# targeted apply leaves rest unrefreshed"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Saved Plans"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -out=tf.plan",
            "terraform apply tf.plan  # exactly reviewed",
            "# plan file embeds the state serial",
            "# fails if state moved on"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interrupt Safety",
          "items": [
            "State is written after each resource, not at the end",
            "An interrupted apply still records what was created",
            "Ctrl-C once = graceful, finishes in-flight work",
            "Ctrl-C twice = hard kill, orphaned resources"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Refresh, Plan, Apply (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Partial Create",
          "text": "Provider returns an ID plus an error. Terraform stores the object and taints it, so the next plan replaces it."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Data sources live in state as `mode: \"data\"`",
            "They are re-read every plan",
            "They never produce create or destroy actions"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Local Backend",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "local disk",
                "lines": [
                  "zero setup",
                  "no sharing",
                  "no locking",
                  "no history"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "remote",
                "lines": [
                  "durable store",
                  "locking",
                  "encryption",
                  "versioning"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A laptop failure loses the mapping outright",
            "Committing state to Git is an anti-pattern",
            "Plaintext secrets land in the history forever",
            "JSON merge conflicts are unresolvable by hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Backend Block Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "terraform {",
            "  backend \"s3\" {",
            "    bucket = \"tf-state\"   # no variables",
            "    key = \"prod/terraform.tfstate\"",
            "    region = \"eu-west-1\"",
            "    encrypt = true",
            "  }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No variables, no interpolation in the block",
            "It is evaluated before the rest of the language",
            "Partial config passes the rest at init time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform init -backend-config=prod.hcl",
            "terraform init \\",
            "  -backend-config=\"key=prod/terraform.tfstate\"",
            "# enable S3 bucket versioning: every write recoverable"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lock Primitives"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Backend",
            "Lock"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "s3 (classic)",
              "DynamoDB `LockID`"
            ],
            [
              "s3 (modern)",
              "`use_lockfile = true`"
            ],
            [
              "azurerm",
              "blob lease"
            ],
            [
              "gcs",
              "object generation"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Local State vs Remote Backends",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "HTTP backend: any REST GET/POST/LOCK/UNLOCK endpoint",
            "That is what GitLab managed state uses",
            "Consul, Kubernetes secrets, Postgres, OSS also exist",
            "Postgres uses advisory locks — good if a DB exists"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The cloud Block"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`cloud {}` replaces the old `remote` backend",
            "Adds remote plan/apply execution and run history",
            "Plus policy enforcement, RBAC and a UI"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Nothing Phones Home",
          "text": "With object backends the CLI reads and writes S3 directly. Only HCP Terraform stores state on their servers."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Option",
            "Lock",
            "Audit",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "local",
              "none",
              "none",
              "free"
            ],
            [
              "S3+DynamoDB",
              "yes",
              "versions",
              "cents"
            ],
            [
              "HCP Terraform",
              "yes",
              "full RBAC",
              "money"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Chicken and Egg",
          "items": [
            "The bucket holding state must exist first",
            "Bootstrap with local state, then migrate",
            "Or create it out-of-band with a script"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`terraform_remote_state` reads another state",
            "It exposes only that state's outputs",
            "A deliberately narrow cross-config interface"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "init Configures the Backend",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Editing the backend block alone does nothing",
            "You get \"Backend initialization required\"",
            "Terraform then offers to copy state over",
            "Confirm the new location before deleting the old"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "migrate vs reconfigure"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`-migrate-state`",
              "copies state across"
            ],
            [
              "`-reconfigure`",
              "discards association"
            ],
            [
              "neither",
              "interactive prompt"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Backend Mechanics and Environments",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The Silent Abandon",
          "text": "`-reconfigure` starts from whatever the new backend already holds. Mixing it up with `-migrate-state` orphans your old state without an error."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Back Up First"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform state pull > backup.tfstate",
            "terraform state push backup.tfstate",
            "# push refuses on lineage mismatch",
            "# or lower serial, unless -force"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Backend credentials use the normal provider chain",
            "Env vars, shared config, instance roles",
            "Resolved separately from the provider block",
            "A provider `assume_role` does not reach the backend"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Environment Separation"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "workspaces",
                "lines": [
                  "one backend",
                  "key per workspace",
                  "cheap",
                  "wrong-workspace risk"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "dir per env",
                "lines": [
                  "separate keys",
                  "separate creds",
                  "more files",
                  "true isolation"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Workspaces: short-lived identical copies, dev sandboxes",
            "Directory-per-env when prod needs other permissions",
            "Or when prod simply has different resources"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keys and Access"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# S3 key that scales with IAM",
            "<team>/<service>/<env>/terraform.tfstate",
            "# workspace prefix defaults to env:",
            "workspace_key_prefix = \"env:\""
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bucket policy grants per-prefix access",
            "Read access to state = read access to every secret",
            "The S3 `key` is not templated per workspace"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Files, Sorted",
          "items": [
            "`.terraform.lock.hcl` — commit it",
            "`.terraform/` — never commit it",
            "`terraform init -backend=false` for CI validate",
            "No credentials needed for that path"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`terraform_remote_state` couples states at read time",
            "SSM Parameter Store or Consul decouples them",
            "Cost: you lose type checking on the values"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Locking and Concurrency",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why Locking Exists",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two applies read the same state at once",
            "Both create resources; the second write wins",
            "First run's resources exist, state never heard of them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "acquire lock",
              "read state",
              "apply",
              "write state",
              "release"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When the Lock Is Taken"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Before anything that writes state",
            "`apply`, `destroy`, `state mv`, `rm`, `push`",
            "And `plan` when the backend persists refresh writes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Lock Info Fields",
          "items": [
            "ID (UUID) and Operation",
            "Who: user@host",
            "Version and Created timestamp",
            "Path to the state object"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Primitives"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Backend",
            "Mechanism"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "DynamoDB",
              "conditional PutItem"
            ],
            [
              "S3 native",
              "`.tflock` If-None-Match"
            ],
            [
              "Azure",
              "blob lease"
            ],
            [
              "GCS",
              "generation precondition"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "DynamoDB LockID item is `<bucket>/<key>`",
            "Condition fails if it exists — mutual exclusion",
            "Table needs only a `LockID` string partition key",
            "On-demand billing costs pennies; also stores a digest"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Flags That Matter"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform apply -lock-timeout=5m  # retry",
            "terraform apply -lock=false      # danger",
            "terraform force-unlock 8c2f1d4a-...",
            "# verify the holder is dead first"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`-lock-timeout` is essential in queued CI pipelines",
            "`-lock=false` is for single-user lockless backends only",
            "Never use it to shove past a stuck lock"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Locking and Concurrency (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stuck Locks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Crashed runs, killed CI jobs, network partitions",
            "The process died before releasing",
            "Read `Who` and `Created` before force-unlocking"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Force-Unlock Is a Loaded Gun",
          "text": "Force-unlocking a still-running apply reintroduces the exact race locking prevents."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Locked state, so we're safe?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Locks protect state writes, not the cloud API",
            "Two states owning one resource still fight",
            "Serialize applies with a CI concurrency group",
            "S3 is strongly consistent since Dec 2020"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "Error acquiring the state lock",
            "Lock Info: ID: 8c2f... Who: ci@runner-3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Drift is any difference between real infrastructure and what state records. It comes from changes made outside Terraform."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Console hotfixes during incidents",
            "Auto-scaling and controllers mutating tags",
            "Cloud provider defaults being applied late",
            "Another IaC tool touching the same resource"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Detection"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -refresh-only",
            "terraform plan -detailed-exitcode",
            "# 0 no changes, 1 error, 2 changes",
            "# nightly job, alert on exit 2"
