          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Read Plans Carefully"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deleted-out-of-band resources vanish on refresh",
            "They reappear as creates, with no error",
            "Rotated passwords cascade into dependent updates",
            "`~` shows drift and config change alike"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only `-refresh-only` isolates world-changed from repo-changed",
            "Prevention beats detection: deny console writes in prod",
            "`prevent_destroy = true` guards the crown jewels",
            "Split large states instead of disabling refresh"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Rule",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "State is keyed by resource address. Renaming a resource or moving it into a module is destroy+create unless you move it in state too."
